---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Base
  title="Hackathon PM Agent | Jeremy Hoover"
  description="In a three-day hackathon I built a set of agent skills that turns a PRD into a checked requirements report. We won Best Use of AI, and it fed into the PM skills and agents teams use now."
>
  <article class="section case-study case-study--violet">
    <header class="case-hero">
      <div class="container case-hero__grid">
        <div class="case-hero__main">
        <a href={`${base}/#projects`} class="back"><span class="back-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Back to selected projects</span></a>
        <h1>I turned a requirements maze into an agent that starts from your PRD</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Every PM had to dig through a wiki, fill out a form, track down contacts, and create work by hand. In a three-day Microsoft hackathon, I built a package of skills and workflows that starts from the PM's PRD instead. The agent pulls out what it can, asks about the rest, and gives the PM a report to check. Nothing else happens until the PM says so.
        </p>

        <div class="outcomes-strip" aria-label="Project outcomes">
          <div class="outcome">
            <span class="outcome__num">Winner</span>
            <span class="outcome__label">Best Use of AI, for our three-person team</span>
          </div>
          <div class="outcome">
            <span class="outcome__num">3 days</span>
            <span class="outcome__label">From idea to working proof of concept</span>
          </div>
          <div class="outcome">
            <span class="outcome__num">Shared</span>
            <span class="outcome__label">Across the PM org, and fed into its skills and agents</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="glance-card" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
          <h2 id="glance-title">At a glance</h2>
          <dl class="glance">
              <div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Senior Content Designer. It was my idea, and I drove it.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Ownership</dt><dd>The skills and workflows, most of the agent instructions, the full interaction, and the demo video</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Team</dt><dd>Three people: me, another designer, and a product manager</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Constraint</dt><dd>Three days, official Microsoft hackathon</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Status</dt><dd>Proof of concept, now part of a larger PM system that's still growing</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Evidence</dt><dd>Best Use of AI, judges' feedback, and wide sharing across PMs. Examples are redrawn with generic content.</dd></div>
            </dl>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="case-body">
      <div class="container case-shell">
        <aside class="disclosure" aria-label="Project disclosure">
          <strong>About the evidence</strong>
          <p>This is internal Microsoft work. I redrew the workflow and conversation with generic content and left out internal requirements, contacts, product details, and work items.</p>
        </aside>

        <nav class="case-toc" aria-label="Hackathon PM agent case study sections">
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#problem">The problem</a></li>
            <li><a href="#decision">The decision</a></li>
            <li><a href="#interaction">How the agent works</a></li>
            <li><a href="#validation">Testing it</a></li>
            <li><a href="#evolution">What happened next</a></li>
            <li><a href="#reflection">What I learned</a></li>
          </ul>
        </nav>

        <section id="problem" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>The problem</h2>
          <p>Every time a PM wanted to turn a product idea into assigned work, they went through the same manual steps.</p>
          <p>They searched a wiki with more than 50 required "fundamentals," filled out a form to figure out which ones applied, tracked down the right groups and contacts, and then created and assigned the work by hand.</p>
          <p>The information was all there. But every PM had to find it, interpret it, and route it again from scratch. The form didn't save any of that work. It just told you where to go look.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="reading-column content-section" aria-labelledby="role-title">
          <h2 id="role-title">My role</h2>
          <p>The idea and the plan were mine. I built the skills and workflows, wrote most of the agent instructions, designed the whole interaction, and made the demo video for our presentation.</p>
          <p>Our PM teammate knew the domain. They walked me through how the wiki, form, requirements, routing, and contacts worked, wrote test PRDs, and helped hook the agent up to our runtime and work tracking.</p>
          <p>So I was the designer and also the one driving the product. I defined the problem, decided how the interaction should work, and took it from idea to demo.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="decision" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>Don't fix the form. Skip it.</h2>
          <p>We looked at keeping the wiki as the main experience, simplifying the form, building a standalone app, and doing a different hackathon idea altogether.</p>
          <p>A shorter form wouldn't have fixed much. The PM already had a PRD with most of the context in it. Making them type it all in again was busywork.</p>
          <p>So we turned the wiki and form into source material for the agent. It starts with the PRD, figures out what it can, and only asks for what's missing. The PM goes from filling in data to checking it.</p>
        </section>

        <figure class="evidence-figure" aria-labelledby="workflow-caption">
          <div class="workflow-compare" role="img" aria-label="Before and after PM workflow comparison showing wiki search, form routing, and manual work creation replaced by a PRD-first verified agent workflow">
            <section class="workflow-panel workflow-panel--before">
              <span class="diagram-label">Before</span>
              <h3>Repeated manual process</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Search 50+ fundamentals</li>
                <li>Complete routing form</li>
                <li>Find groups and contacts</li>
                <li>Create and assign work</li>
              </ol>
            </section>
            <div class="workflow-shift" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
            <section class="workflow-panel workflow-panel--after">
              <span class="diagram-label">After</span>
              <h3>Verified agent workflow</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Provide PRD</li>
                <li>Answer targeted questions</li>
                <li>Verify and save report</li>
                <li>Initiate follow-on actions</li>
              </ol>
            </section>
          </div>
          <figcaption id="workflow-caption">
            <strong>Start with what the PM already has.</strong> The PRD does most of the work. The agent asks only what's missing, then shows a report to confirm.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <section id="interaction" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>How the agent works</h2>
          <p>The agent reads the PRD and pulls out what it can: feature type, release stage, schedule, dependencies, what other teams need, and likely contacts.</p>
          <p>When the PRD doesn't say enough, it asks a specific follow-up question. It never asks the PM for something it already found.</p>
          <p>Then it writes a draft report with:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>The fundamentals that apply</li>
            <li>Where each one came from, or why it applies</li>
            <li>Who to contact</li>
            <li>The basics of each requirement</li>
            <li>The follow-on work it can help set up</li>
          </ul>
          <p>The PM can ask the agent for more detail on anything before confirming.</p>
        </section>

        <figure class="evidence-figure" aria-labelledby="conversation-caption">
          <div class="conversation" aria-label="Generic reconstructed conversation between a product manager and the agent">
            <div class="message message--user"><span>Product manager</span><p>Here is the PRD for a new feature in an upcoming release.</p></div>
            <div class="message message--agent"><span>Agent</span><p>I found the feature type and release stage. Does this experience depend on an existing team capability?</p></div>
            <div class="message message--user"><span>Product manager</span><p>Yes. It uses a shared platform capability.</p></div>
            <div class="report-preview">
              <span>Draft report</span>
              <strong>Applicable fundamental</strong>
              <p>Requirement summary, rationale, responsible contact, and proposed follow-on work.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <figcaption id="conversation-caption">
            <strong>A redrawn example.</strong> The agent combines the PRD with one answer, then shows its reasoning and proposed work for review.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <section class="reading-column content-section" aria-labelledby="confirmation-title">
          <h2 id="confirmation-title">Approving the report isn't approving everything</h2>
          <p>How confirmation works was the most important safety call.</p>
          <p>First the PM checks and confirms the full report. Only then does it get saved. After that, the agent asks about setting up work and other follow-ups one at a time.</p>
          <p>Saying yes to the report doesn't let the agent go do everything. The PM decides each step that matters.</p>
        </section>

        <figure class="evidence-figure" aria-labelledby="agent-flow-caption">
          <ol class="agent-flow">
            <li><span>1</span><strong>Read PRD</strong><small>Extract available context</small></li>
            <li><span>2</span><strong>Infer</strong><small>Find fundamentals, dependencies, and contacts</small></li>
            <li><span>3</span><strong>Ask</strong><small>Only what's missing</small></li>
            <li><span>4</span><strong>Report</strong><small>Show rationale, contacts, and proposed work</small></li>
            <li><span>5</span><strong>Verify</strong><small>PM reviews, corrects, and confirms</small></li>
            <li><span>6</span><strong>Act</strong><small>Start follow-ups one at a time</small></li>
          </ol>
          <figcaption id="agent-flow-caption">
            <strong>Two checkpoints.</strong> The report is approved and saved before the PM picks any follow-on action.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <section id="validation" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>Testing it in three days</h2>
          <p>We ran it against sample PRDs our PM wrote. We checked whether the agent pulled the right context, asked useful questions, and produced a report you could actually work from.</p>
          <p>The judges said it could save PMs hours of wiki searching, form filling, contact hunting, and manual work setup. That's their read on the opportunity, not something we measured in production.</p>
          <p>We won Best Use of AI.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="evolution" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>What happened next</h2>
          <p>What we built in three days was a proof of concept. It's changed a lot since.</p>
          <p>After the hackathon, it was shared across the PM org and fed into a bigger set of PM skills and agents. That work standardized more of the PM workflow across our business group, and multiple teams keep adding to it.</p>
          <p>Our project didn't build all of that on its own. But it was an early piece of it. It showed a different way to handle the fundamentals and gave teams something real to build on.</p>
        </section>

        <div class="evolution-grid" aria-label="Project evolution">
          <div><span>01</span><strong>Proof of concept</strong><small>Working skills and workflows, tested in three days</small></div>
          <div><span>02</span><strong>Wider PM sharing</strong><small>Something real for teams to try and extend</small></div>
          <div><span>03</span><strong>Evolving system</strong><small>Shared skills and agents, built on by multiple teams</small></div>
        </div>

        <section id="reflection" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>What I learned</h2>
          <p>The big call wasn't putting chat on top of a form. It was changing where the work starts: begin with the PRD, ask only what's missing, and get a yes before anything important happens.</p>
          <p>I think it also showed how fast you can get somewhere when the interaction is clear. Three days was enough because we stuck to one repeated problem, one good source of context, and one safe path from understanding to action.</p>
        </section>

        <aside class="closing-panel" aria-labelledby="closing-title">
          <h2 id="closing-title">From busywork to a reusable workflow</h2>
          <p>We took a manual requirements process and turned it into an agent the PM stays in control of. It also helped set the direction for how PMs here use skills and agents day to day.</p>
        </aside>

        <hr class="divider" />
        <nav class="case-pagination" aria-label="Case study navigation">
          <a href={`${base}/work/ai-design-repo`} class="case-pagination__link">
            <span class="case-pagination__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="case-pagination__content"><span class="case-pagination__direction">Previous project</span><span class="case-pagination__title">AI design repository</span></span>
          </a>
          <a href={`${base}/work/org-ai-initiatives`} class="case-pagination__link case-pagination__link--next">
            <span class="case-pagination__content"><span class="case-pagination__direction">Next project</span><span class="case-pagination__title">Org AI initiatives</span></span>
            <span class="case-pagination__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .case-study { padding-top: 0; }
  .tag { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  h1 { margin-block: var(--space-4) var(--space-6); }
  .lede { max-width: 58ch; margin-bottom: var(--space-12); font-size: var(--size-xl); line-height: 1.6; }
  .outcome { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-1); transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .outcome__num { font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 11cqw, 2rem); line-height: 1.1; }
  .outcome__label { max-width: 25ch; font-size: var(--size-sm); color: var(--muted); }
  .case-shell { max-width: calc(var(--narrow) + 6rem); }
  .reading-column { width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin-inline: auto; }
  .content-section { scroll-margin-top: 90px; }
  .content-section h2, .case-summary h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .content-section:not(:first-child) h2 { margin-top: var(--space-16); }
  .content-section p { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .content-section ul { margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-6) var(--space-6); }
  .content-section li { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }

  .disclosure { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 150px 1fr; gap: var(--space-6); width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin: 0 auto var(--space-12); padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--portfolio-blue-soft); border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; }
  .disclosure strong { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.75rem; text-transform: none; }
  .disclosure p { color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--size-sm); }

  .case-meta { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-3); }
  .case-meta div { padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .case-meta dt { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: none; }
  .case-meta dd { color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5; }

  .case-toc { max-width: var(--narrow); margin: var(--space-8) auto var(--space-16); padding-block: var(--space-6); border-block: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .case-toc__label { display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.2; text-transform: none; }
  .case-toc ul { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 0; margin: 0; list-style: none; }
  .case-toc li { --toc-divider: var(--border); display: flex; align-items: center; }
  .case-toc li + li { margin-left: var(--space-4); }
  .case-toc li + li::before { content: ''; width: 2px; height: 16px; margin-right: var(--space-4); border-radius: 999px; background: var(--toc-divider); }
  .case-toc li:nth-child(3n) { --toc-divider: var(--border); }
  .case-toc li:nth-child(3n + 1) { --toc-divider: var(--border); }
  .case-toc a { display: inline-flex; min-height: 32px; align-items: center; color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 650; line-height: 1.3; text-decoration: none; }
  .case-toc a:hover { color: var(--portfolio-blue); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--portfolio-blue); text-decoration-thickness: 2px; text-underline-offset: 5px; }

  .evidence-figure { width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin: var(--space-12) auto var(--space-16); }
  .evidence-figure figcaption { width: 100%; margin-top: var(--space-4); color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--size-sm); }
  .evidence-figure figcaption strong { color: var(--portfolio-ink); }

  .workflow-compare { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--space-3); align-items: stretch; padding: var(--space-4); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; background: #fff; }
  .workflow-panel { padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px; background: var(--portfolio-blue-soft); transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .workflow-panel--before { background: var(--surface-tint); }
  .workflow-panel h3 { margin-block: var(--space-3) var(--space-4); color: var(--portfolio-blue); }
  .workflow-panel ol { margin-left: var(--space-5, 1.25rem); }
  .workflow-panel li { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--size-sm); }
  .diagram-label { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: none; }
  .workflow-shift { display: grid; place-items: center; color: var(--portfolio-blue); font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 800; }

  .conversation { display: grid; gap: var(--space-3); padding: var(--space-4); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; background: var(--portfolio-blue-soft); }
  .message, .report-preview { max-width: 78%; padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-6); border-radius: 14px; background: #fff; transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .message--user { justify-self: end; border-bottom-right-radius: 4px; }
  .message--agent { justify-self: start; border-bottom-left-radius: 4px; }
  .message span, .report-preview > span { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: none; }
  .message p, .report-preview p { margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--size-sm); }
  .report-preview { max-width: 100%; }
  .report-preview strong { display: block; margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--portfolio-ink); }

  .agent-flow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-2); margin: 0; padding: var(--space-4); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; background: var(--surface-tint); list-style: none; }
  .agent-flow li { position: relative; display: flex; min-height: 185px; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-4); border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .agent-flow li > span { display: grid; width: 1.75rem; height: 1.75rem; place-items: center; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--portfolio-blue); color: #fff; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 800; }
  .agent-flow strong { color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.35; }
  .agent-flow small { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.7rem; line-height: 1.45; }

  .evolution-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); gap: var(--space-3); margin: var(--space-8) auto var(--space-16); }
  .evolution-grid div { display: flex; min-height: 165px; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-3); padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px; background: #fff; transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .evolution-grid span { color: var(--portfolio-coral); font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
  .evolution-grid strong { color: var(--portfolio-blue); line-height: 1.35; }
  .evolution-grid small { color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--size-sm); line-height: 1.5; }

  .closing-panel { width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin: var(--space-16) auto 0; padding: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3rem); border-radius: 20px; background: var(--portfolio-blue); }
  .closing-panel .tag { color: var(--portfolio-yellow); }
  .closing-panel h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-3); color: #fff; }
  .closing-panel p { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.82); }
  .divider { margin-block: var(--space-16) var(--space-8); }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .case-toc ul { gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem; }
    .case-toc li + li { margin-left: 0; }
    .case-toc li + li::before { content: none; }
    .agent-flow li { min-height: 150px; }
    .evolution-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .evolution-grid div { min-height: 0; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .content-section { scroll-margin-top: 130px; }
    .disclosure { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-4); }
    .case-meta { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .case-meta div { padding: var(--space-4); }
    .case-toc { margin-top: var(--space-6); margin-bottom: var(--space-12); padding-block: var(--space-4); }
    .case-toc ul { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); width: 100%; gap: var(--space-1) var(--space-6); }
    .case-toc a { min-height: 44px; }
    .workflow-compare { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: var(--space-3); }
    .workflow-shift { transform: rotate(90deg); }
    .message, .report-preview { max-width: 100%; }
    .agent-flow { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: var(--space-3); }
    .agent-flow li { min-height: auto; }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .outcome:hover,
    .case-meta div:hover,
    .workflow-panel:hover,
    .message:hover,
    .report-preview:hover,
    .agent-flow li:hover,
    .evolution-grid div:hover { transform: none; }
  }

  /* ---- Visual refresh ---- */
  /* before / after: two open cards with an arrow badge */
  .workflow-compare { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 48px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--space-4); align-items: center; padding: 0; border: 0; background: transparent; }
  .workflow-panel { height: 100%; padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; background: #fff; box-shadow: none; }
  .workflow-panel--after { border-color: rgba(17,85,204,0.35); background: #fff; box-shadow: var(--elev-2); }
  .diagram-label { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; height: 24px; padding: 0 0.6rem; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--surface-tint); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0; }
  .workflow-panel--after .diagram-label { background: var(--portfolio-blue); color: #fff; }
  .workflow-panel h3 { margin-block: 0.75rem; color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .workflow-panel ul, .workflow-panel ol { margin: 0; list-style: none; }
  .workflow-panel li { position: relative; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; padding-left: 1.6rem; color: var(--text); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .workflow-panel li::before { position: absolute; top: 0.1em; left: 0; display: grid; width: 1.1rem; height: 1.1rem; place-items: center; border-radius: 50%; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1; }
  .workflow-panel--before li { color: var(--muted); }
  .workflow-panel--before li::before { content: '–'; background: #eef0f4; color: var(--muted); }
  .workflow-panel--after li::before { content: '✓'; background: var(--portfolio-blue-soft); color: var(--portfolio-blue); }
  .workflow-shift { display: grid; width: 44px; height: 44px; place-items: center; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--portfolio-blue); box-shadow: var(--elev-2); color: #fff; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .workflow-compare { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .workflow-shift { justify-self: center; transform: rotate(90deg); } }

  /* stepper: numbered nodes on one line */
  .agent-flow { --node: 36px; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.75rem; padding: 0; border: 0; background: transparent; list-style: none; }
  .agent-flow li { position: relative; display: flex; min-height: 0; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; padding: 0; border: 0; border-radius: 0; background: transparent; box-shadow: none; text-align: center; }
